 CODE
Art. 2.3.84.
Data to be entered 
The central register of matrimonial property agreements contains the following data, valid at the time of entry: 
1¡ for each of the spouses who is a party to a deed, declaration or judicial decision as specified in Article 2.3.83, ¤ 1, 1¡, 2¡, 4¡, 5¡ or 6¡, and for each of the legal cohabitants who is a party to the agreement specified in Article 2.3.83, ¤ 1, 3¡: 
a) the surname and first name(s); 
b) the [1 identification number of the National Register or the identification number of the Crossroads Bank for Social Security]; c) the date and place of birth of the legal cohabitant(s).1
c) the date and place of birth; 
d) the domicile or habitual residence; 
2¡ in the cases referred to in Article 2.3.83, ¤ 1, 1¡, 2¡ and 3¡, the nature and date of the document; 
3¡ in the cases referred to in Article 2.3.83, ¤ 1, 1¡, the applicable matrimonial property regime; 
4¡ in the cases referred to in Article 2.3.83, ¤ 1, 4¡, 5¡ and 6¡, the subject matter and date of the judgment or decree; 
5¡ in the cases referred to in Article 2.3.83, ¤ 1, 4¡, 5¡ and 6¡, an indication of any opposition, appeal or recourse against a judgment or decree; 
6¡ identification of the notary, public authority or person who drew up the document or who received the document with a view to its deposit, or of the court which pronounced the judgment or decree;   
7¡ where applicable, the NABAN reference of the document, as referred to in Article 18 of the Law of 16 March 1803 on the organisation of the notarial profession and, failing this, the register number; 
8¡ where applicable, the reference of the judgment or ruling according to the ECLI (European Case Law Identifier) standard, or, failing this, the general roll number of the judgment or ruling; 
9¡ where applicable, the place and date of death of one of these parties.
2 The central register of matrimonial agreements serves as the authentic source of the data entered therein.
